Where a third-party term requires a notice, attribution, source offer or other
condition, you remain responsible for satisfying it when your use or
distribution triggers that condition.

## 16. Separate written permission

The Licensor may give a person separate written permission which permits
Commercial Use, waives or modifies a restriction, or grants additional rights.
That permission overrides this Licence only:

- for the recipient or recipients it identifies;
- for the Software, conduct and period it covers; and
- to the extent it expressly differs from this Licence.

Unless the written permission says otherwise, all unaffected terms of this
Licence continue to apply. Permission given to one recipient does not amend the
public Licence or grant the same permission to anyone else.

The legal terms applicable to a recipient may therefore consist of:

1. this Licence;
2. an applicable `AWOO-SUPPORTER-SYSTEM.md` and
   `AWOO-ASSETS-DEFINITION.md`, but only for the project-specific matters which
   this Licence allows those files to define; and
3. separate written permission expressly granted by the Licensor to that
   recipient.

An informal comment, community post, README statement or other documentation
does not modify this Licence unless it clearly records written permission from
the Licensor and identifies the permission being granted.

## 17. Applicable project version and later upstream changes

A Derivative Work is not required to pull, merge, adopt, track or update to any
later change or release of the Original Project.

For original material incorporated into a Derivative Work, supporter and asset
definitions are determined by the companion files supplied with the upstream
version of that material which the Derivative Work incorporated. Deleting or
changing those definitions in the Derivative Work does not erase obligations
which attached to the incorporated original material.

If a Derivative Work incorporates a later upstream version, it may rely on that
version's express retirement, graduation or reclassification of a Supporter
Feature for the material which the later version updates or supersedes. A later
definition does not retroactively change an older Derivative Work which has not
incorporated that later upstream material, and it does not erase restrictions
on older original material which the Derivative Work retains without the later
replacement.

Nothing in this Licence requires a Derivative Work to grant its changes back to
the Licensor. An intentional submission to the Original Project is governed by
section 14.

An Original Project adopts only the exact version of the Awoo Licence which it
identifies. Awoo Licence v1.0, this Licence, and any future version are separate
licences. There is no automatic upgrade, migration or "or later version"
permission.

## 18. Termination and cure

Your permissions under this Licence terminate automatically when you materially
breach it.

If you fully cure the material breach within 30 days after the earlier of your
discovery of it or your receipt of notice from the Licensor, your permissions
are automatically reinstated from the date of cure, unless the next paragraph
applies. Cure includes stopping the breach and, so far as reasonably possible,
correcting its continuing effects.

For repeated or deliberate material breach, the Licensor may notify you in
writing that automatic reinstatement is unavailable or that your permissions
are permanently revoked. In that case, reinstatement requires the Licensor's
express written permission. The Licensor is not required to treat any fixed
number of breaches as repeated and is not required to take legal action in
order for termination under this section to have effect.

Termination of your permissions does not terminate permissions already received
under this Licence by a person to whom you previously Distributed a compliant
copy or Derivative Work, provided that person remains in compliance.

