## 21. Severability

If any provision of this Licence is held invalid or unenforceable, it is to be
limited or reformed only to the minimum extent necessary to make it valid and
enforceable where the law permits. If it cannot be so limited or reformed, that
provision is severed. The remaining provisions continue in effect.

## 22. No waiver

A delay or failure by the Licensor to enforce a provision or respond to a breach
does not waive that provision, waive any later breach, or prevent later
enforcement. A waiver applies only where the Licensor gives it expressly in
writing and only to the circumstances it identifies.
